From 97e31706e6b05e65cca5ae2028991d19b34ba376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cyberneticangel <cyberneticangel@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:45:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Renderer: skip clean regions in upload scans
 (PERF-153), obtain sizes in DIAG-109, opt-in write scan (PERF-154)

PERF-153: a 16 MB region found clean by a whole-region upload scan in the
current upload epoch is not walked again until a page is marked. Binds of
huge read-only buffers walked every region they cover (GT Sport's race:
~25,000 binds over 256 MB a second); race 20 -> ~50 fps with PERF-117.

PERF-154 (Linux, SHADGT_WRITE_SCAN=1, experimental): CPU writes found with
userfaultfd asynchronous write protection and PAGEMAP_SCAN at each upload
epoch. Too slow as it is (a scan walks all registered memory, ~4 ms, at
~230 epochs a second) and the loading screen stalled for 52 s.
